      "id": "h6i48ao",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Composition of the Atmosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Earth's atmosphere is structurally divided into five distinct layers: Troposphere, Stratosphere, Mesosphere, Thermosphere, and Exosphere.",
        "The Troposphere is the lowest and most vital layer for life, housing almost all atmospheric water vapor and weather phenomena.",
        " reached inside the Stratosphere contains the critical ozone layer that absorbs harmful ultraviolet (UV) radiation.",
        "The Mesosphere sits above the Stratosphere and is where most meteorites burn up upon entering the atmosphere.",
        "The Thermosphere contains the Ionosphere, which reflects radio waves back to Earth, enabling wireless communication."
      ],
      "id": "j8oipa4"
    },
